# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A sigil with text after its closer reads inline, as the memetic plug-in builds it"

# THE MEMETIC BLOCK/INLINE LAW (Train R, operator-approved 2026-11-01). A sigil counts as a block
# only where its `>>` ends the line; with text after it, the line is a paragraph holding an inline
# sigil, the same split TiddlyWiki draws for any call. Collided against the plug-in at Train R's
# aa0a308: `<<~ x a=`v`>>;abc` builds a paragraph (inline lar-sigil, then the text ";abc"), and the
# same sigil alone on its line builds a block.

<<~ x a=`v`>>;abc
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.call.inline.tiddlywiki5
#            ^ - markup.list.unnumbered.term.dl.dt.tiddlywiki5

<<~ ahu slot=`#/x`>> tail
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.call.inline.tiddlywiki5

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///a.b.c`>> tail
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.call.inline.tiddlywiki5

# CONTROLS: a sigil alone on its line stays a block, the ETX foot carrying its seal as `bcc=` among them.

<<~ set from=`lar:///a.b.c` to=`?`>>
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.variable.call.block.tiddlywiki5

<<^ code=`&#x0003;` bcc=`ni:///sha-256;7uFf47o8VMhpXmwKCHt2Ev8Kyin9lwMX-N3DlYeX73k`>>
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.variable.call.block.tiddlywiki5
